  "response": "The environment variable that changes where Ollama stores downloaded models on Windows is `OLLAMA_MODELS`. You can set this variable to specify a different directory for model storage. Here are the steps:\n\n1. Start the Settings (for Windows 11) or Control Panel (for Windows 10) application and search for \"environment variables.\"\n2. Click on \"Edit environment variables for your account.\"\n3. Edit or create a new variable named `OLLAMA_MODELS` and set it to the desired directory path where you want the models to be stored.\n4. Click OK/Apply to save the changes.\n\nAfter setting this variable, if Ollama is already running, you should quit the application and restart it from the Start menu or open a new terminal session. This ensures that the changes take effect.",
